(4916936, 711336, 48560, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by IreneM:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by crayon:</b></div><hr/><i> besides the title being a related to maths, dont really see anything mathematical on the photo itself. what did i miss here anyway? perhaps someone would PM me and tell me more, thank you!<br/> <br/>crayon<br/> <br/>p/s: congrats on the ribbon though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It''s been a (very ;-) long time since I went to school but I do remember that geometry is the mathematics of shape and space. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>you''re right - mathematics exists all around us. in fact, everything around us are designed with mathematical calculations. but we never see them and think of maths (or geometry) because they are not given mathematical names. they say they phi is everywhere</td>', 'Originally posted by IreneM: Originally posted by crayon: besides the title being a related to maths, dont really see anything mathematical on the photo itself. what did i miss here anyway? perhaps someone would PM me and tell me more, thank you! crayon p/s: congrats on the ribbon though.  It''s been a (very ;-) long time since I went to school but I do remember that geometry is the mathematics of shape and space.   you''re right - mathematics exists all around us. in fact, everything around us are designed with mathematical calculations. but we never see them and think of maths (or geometry) because they are not given mathematical names. they say they phi is everywhere', '2008-08-28 00:30:00.000000', NULL, 0),
