(4922358, 711512, 88136, '<td valign="top">greetings from the critique club :D<br/> <br/>i will start off with my first impression of this photo. i gave it a 5 in voting because it seems like a pretty average photo. some areas are a bit noisy, which detracts points(in my book) but the intersting angle adds a few points, so it evened out to average.<br/> <br/>as i said before, i like your setup, but this just isn''t popping out at me. perhaps a differemt lighting, maybe brighter eye catching objects on the shelves.</td>', 'greetings from the critique club :D i will start off with my first impression of this photo. i gave it a 5 in voting because it seems like a pretty average photo. some areas are a bit noisy, which detracts points(in my book) but the intersting angle adds a few points, so it evened out to average. as i said before, i like your setup, but this just isn''t popping out at me. perhaps a differemt lighting, maybe brighter eye catching objects on the shelves.', '2008-08-30 23:46:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4922446, 710682, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review<br/> <br/>Color Saturation and Hue:  Colors are rich, but not over saturated.  Hues are realistic<br/> <br/>Brightness and Contrast: Details are held in the highlights, colors are bright and fresh.  Shadow under the shell, may be a tiny bit harsh.  A little slower fade to black might be welcome to the eye.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  Focus is nice and sharp. Depth of field is a little shallow.  The soft foreground is not bad, but the shell itself goes soft, from about the 12 to 4 o''clock area along the edge, and a little to the interior.  A smaller aperature would fix this easily.<br/> <br/>I like the soft blurry clouds of the sky, but the sky is bright enough to compete with the shell a bit.  As this is an advanced editing challenge, darkening the sky just a little would be well within the rules.<br/> <br/>As is, this is a very good photo and a nice example of nature''s math.</td>', 'Critique Club Review Color Saturation and Hue:  Colors are rich, but not over saturated.  Hues are realistic Brightness and Contrast: Details are held in the highlights, colors are bright and fresh.  Shadow under the shell, may be a tiny bit harsh.  A little slower fade to black might be welcome to the eye. Focus and depth of field:  Focus is nice and sharp. Depth of field is a little shallow.  The soft foreground is not bad, but the shell itself goes soft, from about the 12 to 4 o''clock area along the edge, and a little to the interior.  A smaller aperature would fix this easily. I like the soft blurry clouds of the sky, but the sky is bright enough to compete with the shell a bit.  As this is an advanced editing challenge, darkening the sky just a little would be well within the rules. As is, this is a very good photo and a nice example of nature''s math.', '2008-08-31 00:34:39.000000', NULL, 0),
